<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>Korean Missile Crisis, 2021</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY text=#dcdcdc bgColor=#2b2b2b scroll=auto&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;CMO: The Korean Missile Crisis, 2021&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;Al "Beirutdude" Sandrik&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;The Time Is: 20 January 2021 18:00:00 Zulu/20 October 00:00:00 Abu Dubai Time&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;Last Edited: 14 October 2020&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;Korean Peninsula&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;Playable as the U.S. - Japan Side&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;EM&gt;Up to &lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;24&amp;nbsp;hours in duration&lt;/P&gt;&lt;B&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Background:&lt;/B&gt; (NOTE: This is simply a storyline for the scenario, not what I believe will happen.)&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT color=red&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Note:&lt;/STRONG&gt; I have noted a distint slowdown if NKPA Missiles launch, I looks like the game locks up but it is still working. I assume the MRBM and ABM boost phase calculations are large and when both are occuring simultaniously it slows things way down? For these reasons the USN/JMSDF RIM-161C/E SM-3 SAMs have had automatic fire disabled. You must manually fire them. My advice after 17:00 utc, save early, save often! &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;31 October 2020: The U.S. Election’s "October Surprise" came on Halloween night when the DPRK lunched its new ICBM from its huge Transport-Erector-Launcher (TEL) from a deep valley in the northern DPRK. The missile’s trajectory took it over the North Pole with an object (warhead?) splashing down in the Atlantic Ocean southeast of Bermuda. DPRK state television quickly went on air announcing, "The glorious achievement our Dear Leader, Kim Jong Un, and his strategy of stalling President Trump while a fully functional ICBM missile and warhead, capable of destroying New York City, had been achieved. Now the "Imperialist Dotard" quakes in fear at the sound of our missiles!" Western analysists were split as to whether a warhead was actually tested, or just a weight, but one thing was now clear, the U.S. east coast was in striking range of the new missile.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;3 November 2020: Joe Biden wins the popular vote and several of the battleground states apparently achieving an Electoral College victory, but President Trump refuses to concede claiming, "Voter fraud on a scale unprecedented in American history has occurred." &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;4 November 2020: Trump supporters take to the streets and are countered by leftist protests in the streets of several American cities such as Portland, Seattle, Chicago and Detroit. Several Pro-Trump militia groups declare they will support Trump to the last drop of their blood.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;5-10 November 2020: GOP representatives in battleground states won by Biden try to install Trump supporting Electors for the upcoming Electoral Congress. Democratic legal teams contest the attempt in the lower courts.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;10-20 November 2020: With no resolution to the deepening political crisis, widespread protests and riots break out. The Dallas Massacre, on the 20th, results in 21 dead and 102 wounded when a right-wing militia group fires into a protesting crowd. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;21 November 2020: In a Politburo meeting, in Pyongyang, it is decided the time is right for the reunification of the peninsula. Preparations would be made to take maximum advantage of the growing unrest in America. In fact, NKPA cyber units would be used the further sow discord in the United States and the West.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;22 – 30 November 2020: Following the Dallas Massacre, several other major gunfights erupt between left- and right-wing groups. Governors in many states declare "States of Emergency" with National Guard units taking control of the streets and FBI and State Police raiding many left- and right-wing groups. Facebook and Twitter block the most inflammatory of posts, intercepting many Russian, PRC and DPRK cyber-attacks.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;1 December 2020: Lower courts rule in favor of the Democratic position on the selection of Electors for the, now delayed, Electoral College.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;2 December 2020: In emergency session the Supreme Court hears arguments in the Electoral College case.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;4 December 2020: in a 5-4 ruling the Supreme Court rules in the Democratic favor forcing states where the popular vote went to Joseph Biden to choose Electors who are pledged to Biden.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;6 December 2020: The Electoral College chooses Biden with a 292-vote victory, and Joe Biden is officially elected the 46th President of the United States. President Trump refuses to accept the result declaring a "National State of Emergency" due to the "corrupt election."&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;7 December 2020: The Joint Chiefs of Staff, in a rare public press conference, announce that neither Active Duty nor Reserve forces would enforce the President’s State of Emergency and acknowledge Joseph Biden as the President elect. President Trump Tweets that. "the coward Generals have stabbed him in the back." &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;8 December 2020: The Attorney General, holds a press conference announcing the President would accept the results of the election; however, the President goes into seclusion tweeting almost continuously for the next several days, until Twitter finally suspends his account.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;10 December 2020: The DPRK Politburo decides the maximum confusion would occur during the American Inauguration when the new President would be confused and Americans would likely be distracted by civil strife, which they would help ferment.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;12 December 2020 to 18 January 2021: A uneasy tension spreads across the U.S. as conservative and progressive groups/individuals trade accusations and outright fighting breaks out. The nation, and the world, hold their breath as we approach Inauguration Day. NKPA attempts at fermenting strife yield some results but largely are so amateurish that they are&amp;nbsp;generally ignored.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;19 January 2021: A well placed intelligence source embedded in the DPRK hierarchy sends a despite message to their handlers…&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;"The NKPA will attack the ROK on January 21st, coinciding with the American Inauguration. The attack will begin with the launch of four to eight NKPA KN-11 missiles which have been dispersed in the northern DPRK. Their targets will be major American bases on the island of Okinawa and, simultaneously, a missile submarine will launch two missiles on the air and naval bases on Guam. The plan is to unhinge the American conventional defense of the ROK. Kim Jong Un will announce that any nuclear response from the U.S. will result in the use of the ICBM, tested in October, to destroy American cities along the East Coast, it is a bluff, we do not yet posses warheads for those missiles. It is believed the bluff will cause the American response to be held back. The KN-11 missiles have poor accuracy and are subject to malfunction but it is estimated that,&amp;nbsp;at least, two of the weapons are likely to detonate if they reach their targets. Therefore, you must destroy the submarine and the missile launchers before they can launch…"&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;NOTES: &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;DIR&gt;
&lt;DIR&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Please turn on the "Special Message Popup" so you can receive a series of Emergency Action Messages (EAMs). They will prompt you as&amp;nbsp;what National Command knows and&amp;nbsp;their instructions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Each NK Strategic Rocket Forces missile TEL represents a single launcher with a single&amp;nbsp;missile (no reloads, so they are not 6x TEL units as I eliminated 5 TELs per unit). To give the scenario some replay value each TEL has an Individual chance of teleporting, thus an MRBM&amp;nbsp;shell game, just as TELs are supposed to do! Also there are a LOT of "mobile units" to make ID'ing the TELs much more difficult. The TELs may not fire immediately if the NKPA and U.S.-Japan&amp;nbsp;become hostile, but at some point (random time event) they will activate. Conversely the TELs may fire first it just all&amp;nbsp;depends upon how the random actions occur.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The KPAF Air Defense Intercept Zone is roughly 50 miles from the DPRK coast. If you are caught penetraing DPRK airspace the DPRK will consider all of your forces to be hostile (tensions are high!).&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;NCA has directed that you are to exhaust conventional attacks/options before using your nuclear weapons (I think for obvious reasons?)..&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Your RM-161E SM-3 are limited to about two (2) per ABM vessel which is&amp;nbsp;six&amp;nbsp;(6) in total use them carefully. Might want to place them on hold for manual/human launch (Shift + F1).&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;You do have one (1) THAAD CEC battery each with ONLY six (6) missiles each one (1) on&amp;nbsp;Guam and one (1) on Okinawa.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;There are a large amount of IMGSAT and SIGINT satellites in orbit, Japan, UK and USA, you will need them, but they are unlikely to find all of the TELs either!&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/DIR&gt;&lt;/DIR&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Originally created under CMO Version 1.01, Build 1147.14 – Data Base: DB3000 487&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;.INI and .Delta files have both been provided for deep rebuilds&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Al "BeirutDude" Sandrik (ex-Beachinnole)&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Al.Sandrik@gmail.com&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
